two hostages including an American were  freed overnight in a rare prisoner swap  with the Taliban the men had been held  captive for more than three years Holly  Williams is following developments from  Istanbul Turkey hala what are what do we  know about this swap Ali good morning  well Kevin king from Pennsylvania was  the last known living American hostage  being held by the Taliban  he was released today along with an  Australian hostage Timothy weeks  both men were teachers at the American  University in Kabul when they were  kidnapped back in 2016 they appeared in  Taliban hostage videos pleading for  their release during their more than  three years in captivity in a statement  Kevin King's sister said it had been a  quote painful ordeal for the entire  family the Afghan government has  confirmed to CBS News this morning that  the two men were exchanged for three  senior members of the Taliban one of  them is enough Haqqani now he is a key  figure the son of the founder of the  Haqqani network that is a wing of the  Taliban notorious for its brutality and  it's suicide bombings the Taliban has  confirmed today that 10 members of the  Afghan state security forces were also  released as part of this prisoner swap  this prisoner exchange is apparently an  attempt to restart peace talks with the  Taliban and end  Afghanistan's 18 year long war the US  was close to an agreement with the  Taliban back in September but those  negotiations broke down Tony  Holly Williams for us Holly thank you  very much
 

